<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 26 August, from 683 to 1978.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/medina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/683">683 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,343 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Umayyad forces fight the rebels of Medina at al-Harra</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a>'s Umayyad army under Muslim ibn Uqba fought the rebel defenders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> on the lava field of Harrat Waqim, north-east of the city. The battle lasted less than a day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1071">1071 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">955 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alp Arslan defeats and captures Romanos IV at Manzikert</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a> defeated the Byzantine army and captured Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a>. The battle opened Anatolia to Turkish settlement, and Byzantine appeals for help later led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Battle of Manzikert</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1278">1278 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">748 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rudolf I and Ladislaus IV defeat Ottokar II on the Marchfeld</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Dürnkrut and Jedenspeigen, the German king Rudolf I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a>, allied with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</a>, defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a>. The victory gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> to the Habsburgs, who ruled Austria until 1918.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-marchfeld">Battle on the Marchfeld</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany">Rudolf I of Germany</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1346">1346 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">680 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III's longbowmen defeat the French at Crécy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> and dismounted men-at-arms cut down repeated French cavalry charges at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy">Crécy</a>. The victory, with heavy losses among the French nobility, opened the way to the siege of Calais.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1444">1444 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">582 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Dauphin's Armagnacs destroy a Swiss force outside Basel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside Basel, about 1,500 Swiss Confederates attacked a far larger French army of Armagnac <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> under the Dauphin Louis, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a>, and were almost entirely destroyed. Their resistance impressed the Dauphin, who withdrew and made peace.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-jakob-an-der-birs">Battle of St. Jakob an der Birs</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France adopts the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> proclaimed that men are born free and equal in rights, and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> rests with the nation. The declaration became a founding text of modern human rights.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1883">1883 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">143 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Krakatoa begins its cataclysmic eruption</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The volcano of Krakatoa in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda Strait</a> began its climactic eruption, culminating in explosions the next day heard thousands of kilometres away. Tsunamis killed more than 36,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda Strait</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 19th Amendment is certified, giving US women the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State Bainbridge Colby certified the 19th Amendment, barring denial of the vote on account of sex. It crowned a campaign launched at Seneca Falls in 1848.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1978">1978 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">48 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albino Luciani is elected Pope John Paul I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> became the first pope to take a double name, honouring his two predecessors. Known as the 'smiling pope', he died after just 33 days.</p></div></li></ol>
